  "title": "Why does STM32MP257F-DK not having EMI-filters on RX lines for USB 3.0?",
  "content": "<p>Why does STM32MP257F-DK not having EMI-filters on RX lines for USB 3.0?</p><p>Can it be like a common standard that the transmitter TX should always have:</p><ul><li>AC capacitors</li>\t<li>ESD protection</li>\t<li>EMI-filtering</li></ul><p>And the RX does not need anything of those, because it’s assuming that their transmitter already having these implemented?</p><p>This picture is from mb1605-mp257f-c01-schematic.pdf</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/1afbef68-b316-4d45-82d2-48feeea6ba5f.png\" /></figure><p> </p>",
